        skos:definition        "The ocean mixed layer is the upper part of the ocean, regarded as being well-mixed. Various criteria are used to define the mixed layer; this can be specified by using a standard name of ocean_mixed_layer_defined_by_X. \"Thickness\" means the vertical extent of a layer."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0467";
