        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Th\" means the element \"thorium\" and \"231Th\" is the isotope \"thorium-231\" with a half-life of 1.06e+00 days."@en;
