<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A63/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV16A63";
        dc:date                "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV16A63";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A63/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV16A63/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_sea_ice_amount_due_to_surface_melting/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_sea_ice_amount_due_to_surface_melting>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/CRYS/>;
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. \"Amount\" means mass per unit area. \"Sea ice\" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs. The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV16A63";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_sea_ice_amount_due_to_surface_melting"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/J63A1HOU/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::J63A1HOU";
        dc:date                "2017-06-26 15:24:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::J63A1HOU";
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-06-26 15:24:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/J63A1HOU/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/steric_change_in_mean_sea_level/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/steric_change_in_mean_sea_level>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Steric sea level change is caused by changes in sea water density due to changes in temperature (thermosteric) and salinity (halosteric). \"Mean sea level\" means the time mean of sea surface elevation at a given location over an arbitrary period sufficient to eliminate the tidal signals. Zero mean sea level change is an arbitrary level. The sum of the quantities with standard names thermosteric_change_in_mean_sea_level and halosteric_change_in_mean_sea_level has the standard name steric_change_in_mean_sea_level."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::J63A1HOU";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "steric_change_in_mean_sea_level"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/ULAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/Q2MSMD99/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::Q2MSMD99";
        dc:date                "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::Q2MSMD99";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/Q2MSMD99/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/Q2MSMD99/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/nudging_increment_in_mass_content_of_water_in_soil/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/nudging_increment_in_mass_content_of_water_in_soil>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "A \"nudging increment\" refers to an amount added to parts of a model system. The phrase \"nudging_increment_in_X\" refers to an increment in quantity X over a time period which should be defined in the bounds of the time coordinate. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Water\" means water in all phases. The mass content of water in soil refers to the vertical integral from the surface down to the bottom of the soil model. For the content between specified levels in the soil, standard names including \"content_of_soil_layer\" are used."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::Q2MSMD99";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "nudging_increment_in_mass_content_of_water_in_soil"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/UWZBT8RK/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
