        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"F\" means the element \"fluorine\" and \"18F\" is the isotope \"fluorine-18\" with a half-life of 6.98e-02 days."@en;
