        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Zr\" means the element \"zirconium\" and \"93Zr\" is the isotope \"zirconium-93\" with a half-life of 3.47e+08 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::2370TTAP";
