        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Sm\" means the element \"samarium\" and \"149Sm\" is the isotope \"samarium-149\" with a half-life of 3.65e+18 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::GO7NJBSV";
