<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/RDW2L4X3/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::RDW2L4X3";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::RDW2L4X3";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/RDW2L4X3/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/radioactivity_concentration_of_209Bi_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/radioactivity_concentration_of_209Bi_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Bi\" means the element \"bismuth\" and \"209Bi\" is the isotope \"bismuth-209\" with a half-life of 7.29e+20 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::RDW2L4X3";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_209Bi_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/6PKIBDQJ/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::6PKIBDQJ";
        dc:date                "2018-12-17 17:17:12.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::6PKIBDQJ";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-12-17 17:17:12.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/6PKIBDQJ/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/6PKIBDQJ/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/6PKIBDQJ/2/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_hydrogen_peroxide_due_to_wet_deposition/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_hydrogen_peroxide_due_to_wet_deposition>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including \"content_of_atmosphere_layer\" are used. The mass is the total mass of the molecules. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Wet deposition\" means deposition by precipitation. The chemical formula for hydrogen peroxide is H2O2."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::6PKIBDQJ";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_hydrogen_peroxide_due_to_wet_deposition"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/KQ6S1BDW/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::KQ6S1BDW";
        dc:date                "2023-02-06 17:17:13.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::KQ6S1BDW";
        pav:authoredOn         "2023-02-06 17:17:13.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/KQ6S1BDW/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_concentration_of_organic_carbon_in_pm2p5_dry_aerosol_particles_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_concentration_of_organic_carbon_in_pm2p5_dry_aerosol_particles_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Mass concentration\" means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction \"mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. Aerosol particles take up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the particles. \"Dry aerosol particles\" means aerosol particles without any water uptake. \"Pm2p5 aerosol\" means atmospheric particulate compounds with an aerodynamic diameter of less than or equal to 2.5 micrometers. Chemically, \"organic carbon aerosol\" refers to the carbonaceous fraction of particulate matter contained in any of the vast number of compounds where carbon is chemically combined with hydrogen and other elements like O, S, N, P, Cl, etc. In measurements of carbonaceous aerosols, organic carbon samples may also include some inorganic carbon compounds, whose mass is neglected and assumed to be distributed between the elemental and organic carbon components of the aerosol particles. Reference: Petzold, A., Ogren, J. A., Fiebig, M., Laj, P., Li, S.-M., Baltensperger, U., Holzer-Popp, T., Kinne, S., Pappalardo, G., Sugimoto, N., Wehrli, C., Wiedensohler, A., and Zhang, X.-Y.: Recommendations for reporting \"black carbon\" measurements, Atmos. Chem. Phys., 13, 8365-8379, https://doi.org/10.5194/acp-13-8365-2013, 2013."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::KQ6S1BDW";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_concentration_of_organic_carbon_in_pm2p5_dry_aerosol_particles_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UKMC/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/T6UW68QE/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
