        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"U\" means the element \"uranium\" and \"230U\" is the isotope \"uranium-230\" with a half-life of 2.08e+01 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::T811AIWV";
