        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Br\" means the element \"bromine\" and \"84mBr\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"bromine-84\" with a half-life of 4.16e-03 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::8WRYPCHA";
